    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and the standalone `checkDigit` into a single stored `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`.\n\n**New single source of truth** \u2014 `model/MemberId.java` (replaces `CustomerCode.java`):\n- `forOwner(owner)` builds `region + FY(2-digit) + HASH8(8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over telephone+lastName) + CHK`, where CHK is `CheckDigit.luhn(...)` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n- `deduplicate(...)` keeps the collision handling (now on the memberId, appending `-<n>`).\n- `region(...)` parses the region back out by stripping the fixed 11-char `FY+HASH8+CHK` tail (and any dedup suffix) \u2014 robust regardless of region length.\n\n**Wiring / consumers updated:**\n- `Owner` entity: `customerCode`/`customer_code` field+column \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` (getter/setter renamed).\n- `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignOwnerMemberId`; pipeline step `assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `assignMemberId` in `owners.POST.yml`. It still runs after telephone-normalize and registration-date-resolve, so the hash and FY inputs are ready.\n- `OwnerMapper`: removed `membershipNumber()` and `checkDigit()` methods + their `@Mapping`s; `memberId` now auto-maps from the stored field; `locality()` derives the region from `MemberId.region(memberId)`; the inbound `ignore` target renamed to `memberId`.\n- Audit record: `OwnerCreatedEvent.customerCode` \u2192 `memberId`; `AuditOwnerCreated` log line now emits `memberId` (dropped the derived `membershipNumber`).\n- Owner segment: unchanged code, now sourced from `memberId` via `locality()`.\n- `openapi.yml`: replaced the three properties with a single `memberId`; updated the `locality` description.\n- All four `schema.sql` files: `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`.\n- Doc comments on `CheckDigit`, `FiscalYear`, `Sha256` updated to reference the member id.\n\n**Verification:** full suite green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` confirms the `NSW\u2026`-prefixed id contains the expected HASH8 and that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone. A sample emitted id: `NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW \u00b7 FY27 \u00b7 `16E6609E` \u00b7 CHK `1`).",
